{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/semirings\/semiring"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Semiring"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SQ","text":"Equatable"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"⊗ extends a path by an edge and ⊕ combines alternative paths. The shortest-path entry points in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ShortestPaths answer a different question for each conformer. The tropical semiring gives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shortest paths, the bottleneck semiring widest paths, the Boolean semiring reachability, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counting semiring the number of paths.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A conformer implements the four requirements. The type system does not check the laws, and an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithm’s result is meaningful only when they hold:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊕ is associative and commutative, with identity "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zero"},{"type":"text","text":";"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊗ is associative, with identity "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"one"},{"type":"text","text":";"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" annihilates: ","type":"text"},{"code":"a ⊗ 0̄ == 0̄ ⊗ a == 0̄","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":";","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊗ distributes over ⊕ from both sides."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊗ need not be commutative. Algorithms always compute "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distance ⊗ weight"},{"type":"text","text":", in path order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is not ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdditiveArithmetic.zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". No semiring type here is a number, and a tropical","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"zero","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is +∞.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The operators ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"⊕"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"⊗"},{"text":" call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plus(_:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"times(_:)"},{"text":", so the two spellings always agree.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Prefer the methods where another module might declare the same operators, and inside","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"text":". That macro folds an expression without these operators’ precedences, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect(a ⊕ b == c)"},{"text":" does not type-check, while ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect(a.plus(b) == c)"},{"text":" does.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"anchor":"Operators","title":"Operators","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/_(_:_:)-2ou28","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/_(_:_:)-93rtg"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"